comments[13]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-21T22:32:32.412Z",codex-root,"Historical delivery evidence is preserved by the item title, parent lineage, release metadata, generated changelog, and repository verification gates."
  "2026-07-23T04:53:19.528Z",codex-root,"Live failure evidence: Auto Release run 29894239662 passed all preparation and release gates, published 2026.7.22, then child Release run 29894284980 failed its immediate npx lookup with npm ETARGET. GitHub issue #43 records the scheduled failure."
  "2026-07-23T04:59:41.948Z",codex-root,"Implementation checkpoint: workflow delegates to the bounded registry verifier; exact npx and bunx version output is asserted; bin paths publish without npm correction warnings; TOON spec marker and encoder dependency are 4.0; repo-local pm-cli is 2026.7.22."
  "2026-07-23T04:59:41.948Z",codex-root,"Quality proof: 20 test files and 934 tests pass with 100% statements (4636/4636), branches (3389/3389), functions (521/521), and lines (4336/4336). TypeScript, type-aware ESLint, Prettier, 20/20 module docstrings, jscpd, ShellCheck, and Bun audit are green."
  "2026-07-23T05:00:12.837Z",codex-root,"The direct release:check correctly rejected already-tagged 2026.7.22 on 2026-07-23. Pre-release validation must use release:pipeline:dry-run, which computes the next calendar version before invoking the full release checks and restores all generated files."
  "2026-07-23T05:03:50.031Z",codex-root,The calendar-aware dry run upgraded the committed project pm-changelog runtime from 2026.7.18 to the registry-latest 2026.7.22. This is required by the request and makes subsequent dry runs clean and deterministic; generated extension artifacts are retained as project-owned release tooling.
  "2026-07-23T05:14:49.412Z",codex-root,"CodeRabbit exact-head review found a valid substring-match weakness in published consumer verification. Replaced includes() with an exact trimmed-line predicate shared by npx and bunx checks, added prefix/suffix/CRLF/multiline regression coverage, and documented the verifier helpers. The reported duplicate parsed declaration is not present at current head: the TOON v4 test contains one declaration and passes compilation."
  "2026-07-23T05:25:06.579Z",codex-root,"Final pre-close evidence: clean-calendar release pipeline dry run computed v2026.7.23, regenerated the PM changelog, passed version/tag/history-secret gates, built the package, ran 935 tests at 100/100/100/100, and passed npx plus bunx package smoke. PR #44 exact head acfdca8 has all repository checks green and zero unresolved review threads; CodeRabbit confirmed the fix and withdrew its stale finding."
  "2026-07-27T22:25:59.682Z",codex-searxng-agent,"Post-publication discovery: npm tarball 2026.7.27 contains source-status and a direct extracted/local build reports current, but npm exec resolves /home/linuxbrew/.linuxbrew/lib/node_modules/searxng-cli/dist/searxng-cli.js, whose help omits source-status. The existing verifier only asserts a version line, so same-version global leakage passed Release run 30310208127."
  "2026-07-27T22:28:57.748Z",codex-searxng-agent,"Implementation replaces opportunistic npx/bunx resolution with separate exact-version npm and Bun installs, realpath containment assertions for both searxng shims, no-install execution, exact version lines, and source-status help probes. This makes the immutable 2026.7.27 artifact a regression fixture and prevents same-version global leakage."
  "2026-07-27T22:31:23.476Z",codex-searxng-agent,"Acceptance checkpoint: bun run quality passed 949 tests at exact 100/100/100/100; bun run test:release, the isolated immutable 2026.7.27 npm/Bun verifier, and npm pack dry-run passed. The linked release:pipeline:dry-run intentionally stopped at its clean-tree guard because implementation and PM evidence were uncommitted; it will be rerun from a clean commit as the calendar-policy proof."
  "2026-07-27T22:33:59.625Z",codex-searxng-agent,"Clean acceptance matrix passed 5/5 through pm test. release:pipeline:dry-run returned release_already_cut_today for immutable v2026.7.27, correctly preventing a second same-day tag; the already-published artifact itself passed both isolated executable and source-status contract probes. PM validate has no integrity, drift, file, dependency, or storage errors (one expected warning because this reopened issue retains its closed parent); graph audit reports 57 nodes, 167 edges, and zero findings; package doctor reports all 12 managed extensions active and current."
  "2026-07-27T23:00:24.687Z",codex-searxng-agent,"CodeRabbit review on PR #57 found a valid test-quality gap: source-text assertions could not prove helper behavior. Extracted shim containment and source-status parsing into a directly imported release module, then added real symlink containment success/escape failure cases plus missing and misleading help-output cases. Focused release tests now pass 12/12."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-23T04:53:19.528Z",codex-root,Use the existing scripts/release/verify-published-release.mjs bounded registry wait as the single consumer-verification owner; remove duplicated inline workflow logic to prevent contract drift.
learnings[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-07-23T04:53:19.528Z",codex-root,Publishing success does not imply immediate registry read-after-write consistency. Exact-version consumer verification must wait for npm view to expose the version before invoking npx or bunx.
